-- title:
--   Trace zero on inertia coinvariants in the supersingular case
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and $N \ge 1$ an integer with $p \mid N$ but $p^2 \nmid N$, and let $S_0$ be a finite set of natural numbers with $p \notin S_0$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and has finite residue field, and suppose $p$ lies in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S_0$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S_0$, to $\mathcal{O}'$. Assume $\chi(U_p)$ is not a unit and that $p = \chi(U_p)\beta$ for some non-unit $\beta \in \mathcal{O}'$. Let $k$ be a field, $\psi : k \to \mathcal{O}'/\mathfrak{m}$ a ring homomorphism, and $\bar\rho$ a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ trivial on the elements fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no stable subspace other than $0$ and the whole space. Assume there is a finite set $S$ of natural numbers such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $P$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ pushed forward along $\psi$ equals $X^2 - \overline{\chi(T_\ell)}X + \ell$. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$, assume some $\tau$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ has $\bar\rho(\tau) \ne 1$, let $\sigma$ be a Frobenius element at $p$ for $P$ in the above sense, and let $E$ be a $k$-endomorphism of $V / \sum_{\tau \in I_P} \operatorname{im}(\bar\rho(\tau) - 1)$ induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ on classes. Then $\operatorname{tr}_k E = 0$.
--
--   This is the supersingular case of the local analysis at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level in level lowering, as in Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, §4.2: when both $\chi(U_p)$ and $p/\chi(U_p)$ fail to be units, the inertia coinvariants at $p$ of the associated residual representation carry no Frobenius trace (indeed the coinvariant space vanishes, so every endomorphism of it has trace zero). It is used in the construction of ring homomorphisms out of Hecke algebras with prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials, in particular in the statements producing an eigensystem at level away from $p$.
